 flag←AcreIsAvailable
⍝ Returns 1 if acre is available, and 0 otherwise.\\
⍝ Note that acre may well be installed as a user command without `⎕SE.acre` being around yet:
⍝ executing `]acre.Version` is what materialises it, hence the probe.\\
⍝ Since that probe is expensive - and, when acre is not installed at all, expensive on every
⍝ single call - the answer is cached in the global `∆ACRE_IS_AVAILABLE`. Expunge that variable
⍝ in case acre gets installed while the session is already up and running.
 :If 2=⎕NC'∆ACRE_IS_AVAILABLE'
     flag←∆ACRE_IS_AVAILABLE
 :Else
     :If 0=⎕SE.⎕NC'acre'
         :Trap 0
             {}⎕SE.UCMD'acre.Version'
             flag←1
         :Else
             flag←0
         :EndTrap
     :Else
         flag←1
     :EndIf
     ∆ACRE_IS_AVAILABLE←flag
 :EndIf
⍝Done
